# Frontend implementation brief — through PM

TK-S2-DESIGN planning delivery; this file is not an independent assignment or acceptance. PM supplies the full dispatch, accepted candidate SHA and writer lease to @frankzhu94/factory-frontend. Starting design revision `398ebdcbc417400aa32ca510e2546808a43b26ab`; artifacts in `/Users/frank/mygit/Tablekeeper/result-run-3/planning/design/stage-2/`. Read the full interaction specification and tokens, not this brief alone.

Implement the four routes with the shared Tablekeeper shell and restrained restaurant-menu visual system. Heading Georgia, body Trebuchet MS/Segoe UI fallback; ivory background, forest actions, fine rules. Use native labelled inputs, 44px targets and visible blue focus. Time-led wrapping seating cards preserve all required singles in fixture order, then available declared pairs; both member labels dominate pair cards. At 375px stack fields/cards/form, wrap arbitrary labels and forbid page overflow. At desktop use max 1200px content and 340px booking column when selected.

Build reusable shell/field/action/feedback/option/receipt components around the architecture controllers. No domain duplication or invented routes/testids. Use session provider; one immutable detail+availability bundle per accepted search generation; separate selected snapshot and immutable booking attempt; lookup generation guards. Search drafts cannot relabel results. Preserve selected form, inputs and error during 409 refresh even when selected option disappears. Unknown booking outcome uses only booking-uncertain; same exact request/key must retry unchanged. Confirmed response clears error/uncertainty and preserves form. Repeat submit reaches server. Semantic edits invalidate identity; obsolete callbacks cannot take ownership. Singleton payload uses legacy table_id for upgrade compatibility; pair uses declared-order table_ids. Current-user and pending attempts survive between-request import without reload.

All copy/state/focus behavior and exact selector mappings are normative design decisions in interaction-specification.md. Keep no-slots exclusive to empty slot lists; all-unavailable nonempty slots retain the full grid. Confirmation-reference is exactly the reference; status exactly confirmed/cancelled. All summaries/receipts/lookup name every table. Signup/login errors mount auth-error only when present. Unavailable choices use disabled buttons but remain readable. No runtime fonts/CDNs/images, lazy route chunks, polling or cross-tab synchronization.

Preserve Stage 1. Backend owns service selectors/views/migration/serving; Frontend owns assigned web/build integration only when PM grants it. Coordinate package/lockfile changes through PM's one writer. API remains authoritative for time, capacity, occupancy and cancellation. No new auth provider, reservation backend, later-stage features or decorative dependencies.

Before handing actual UI for review, collect implementation checks and give PM the full committed revision, clean status and commands/results. Designer later needs exact candidate and service evidence for desktop/375px screenshots, keyboard focus, long labels, every feedback category, and preserved retry/upgrade behavior. The accompanying checklist is NOT_TESTED, not acceptance. No unresolved architecture conflict was identified in this design pass.

